# Application dates and overdue outreach priority
Workstream-ID: lea-26
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/26
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded hiring-outreach dashboard improvement
Status: DONE
Milestone: Make untouched older applications the first outreach priority
Dependencies: lea-09

## Purpose
Show the recorded application date beside hiring-team outreach and separate
contacts with applications more than seven days old and no outreach yet.
Keep that priority table under the existing header with a red outline, without
changing message delivery or treating drafted messages as sent.

## Tasks
- [x] Inspect application timestamps, outreach state and prior dirty work.
- [x] Expose the matched submitted application's recorded date.
- [x] Split untouched older contacts into an oldest-first red-outlined table.
- [x] Preserve selection, completion, note marking and undo across both tables.
- [x] Qualify fictional dates, boundary conditions and actual browser actions.
- [x] Update affected guides and prepare the scoped completion reconciliation.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Both queues show a read-only application date, not the draft creation date.
- [x] Only applications strictly older than seven days with no connection note sent enter priority.
- [x] The priority table appears first under the same header with a red outline and explicit text.
- [x] Recently applied, note-sent and unknown-date contacts remain in the regular queue.
- [x] Matching application/run identity, time zones and oldest-first ordering are retained.
- [x] Both tables retain native content sizing, profile links and correct completion targets.
- [x] Marking or undoing a connection note reclassifies only the correct contact.
- [x] Qualification uses fictional state and preserves private inputs and independent applications.
- [x] Prior local work, older tracking records and existing releases remain unchanged.
- [x] One repository issue, one issue-backed Project item and a durable backlink represent the workstream.

## Completion evidence
Both native tables show Applied on in local time from the matched submitted
application, preferring completion time and using recorded start only when
completion time is absent. Missing or invalid dates show Unknown and an explicit
warning. Untouched applications strictly older than seven days appear oldest
first in the red-outlined Prioritize first table under the existing heading.
Connection notes already marked sent count as initial outreach, so those pending
full messages stay in the regular queue. Classification refreshes on rerun.

Black, Ruff and scoped mypy pass. All 106 focused dashboard, database, Reports
and outreach cases pass without failures, errors or skips. The original source
genuinely failed the new date/presentation regressions before implementation.
Actual browser qualification passes seven boundaries and twenty successful
backend completions using only six fictional contacts. Both tables retain
read-only dates, native content sizing, profile links, contained scrolling at
600 pixels, resizing and Autosize tested from fresh pages.

A real-browser equal-sized queue swap exposed stale positional selections even
after server-state clearing. Native widget keys now include ordered outreach
IDs. Requalification confirms both old selections clear, Remove with no new
selection deletes nothing, both-table completion deletes exactly the checked
IDs, note/undo reclassifies the correct contact and results survive reload.
Per-contact completion and regular-only/empty states retain application history.
Both final layout screenshots were directly reviewed.

Five affected guides document dates, classification and native identity.
Only owned fixture processes were stopped; their inspected fictional databases
were removed. Prior local improvements, private setup, independent applications
and published releases are outside the fixture and remain preserved.
This is bounded local technical completion, not live qualification, human
acceptance, source publication or a new release. Scoped completion tracking is
independently reconciled separately from this managed description.

